# Requirement status — phase 2 — Expenses, Documents, Projects. Assessed against the code on 2026-09-27.
#
# How to read this file
#   TESTED       engine + screen + a named automated test that asserts the behaviour
#   IMPLEMENTED  engine + screen, workflow works end to end, no test for this specific requirement
#   PARTIAL      some of it works; the note says "Built: ... Not built: ..."
#   PLANNED      not built; listed in PLANNED with the reason
#
# Facts that apply to many entries below (verified in the code):
#   * Expense categories (expense_categories) are used by expense claims only. Bills and journals are
#     classified by ledger. No category is preloaded in a new company; the chart template supplies ledgers.
#   * An expense claim line can be tagged with a department and a project only (src/pages/ClaimEditor.tsx).
#     A bill, invoice or purchase-order line can be tagged with a project only (src/pages/DocumentEditor.tsx).
#     A hand-written journal can carry a vehicle, trip, event, property, office or other tag
#     (src/pages/JournalEditor.tsx). A claim or an advance linked, as a whole, to a trip, a path or an event
#     carries that item's tag into its accounting entry (supabase/migrations/0011_review_corrections.sql,
#     tests/sql/phase2_corrections.sql T135). The claim and advance screens offer trips, paths and events
#     for linking; they do not offer vehicles, properties or incidents.
#   * Records corrected on 2026-09-27 after the review corrections (scripts/_assess/CORRECTIONS.md):
#     133, 186, 195, 197, 198, 212, 215, 231, 266, 294, 295, 296, 665, 1366, 1587, 1588, 1775.
#   * Warnings are shown inside the application (Forward, Registers, Inbox). Nothing is sent by email,
#     SMS, WhatsApp or push, and nothing runs on a timer.
#   * Uploading a file to the live storage bucket and signing in were not exercised against the live system.
